<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moscow Mathematical Papyrus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> Mathematical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papyrus">Papyrus</a> is an ancient Egyptian mathematical text of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-francia">Middle Kingdom</a>, probably of the Thirteenth Dynasty, now in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-pushkin">Pushkin</a> Museum in Moscow. Its 25 problems include the correct calculation of the volume of a truncated pyramid. With the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhind-mathematical-papyrus">Rhind Mathematical Papyrus</a> it is a main source for Egyptian mathematics.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moscow-mathematical-papyrus.jpg" alt="Moscow Mathematical Papyrus" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hieroglyphic transcript is made by I. I. Perepelkin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moskou-papyrus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
